On Aug 2, 2:58 pm, Haakon Studebaker <hepta...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Is he too tough or is he just right considering the skills and patience
> necessary to play a monk?

He's difficult. Not so much tough as very deadly, very quickly.

Ideally, obtain magic resistance and zap him with a wand of death. If
not magic resistance, then at least free action. He's so tough that
I'd advise going to the castle first and getting the wand of wishing
so that you have the MR and a wand of death (and the usual other
things like reflection). Life saving is probably a waste because
usually if Kaen kills you once he'll do it again just as quickly. If
you can't take care of the castle you're not likely to be ready for
Kaen. Hit points are largely irrelevant.

There are cleverer ways to take him out but it's better not to finesse
Kaen if you don't have to.



